hadiths[416]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8491","Abu Matar reports that he saw Ali رضي الله عنه come to a young boy and buy a shirt from him for three dirhams. He wore it, reaching between the wrists and the ankles, and said while wearing it: Praise be to Allah who has provided me from clothing what I beautify myself with among people and conceal my nakedness with. It was asked of him: Is this something you say on your own, or do you narrate it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: This is something I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say at the time of wearing new clothes. > **""Praise be to Allah who has provided me from clothing what I beautify myself with among people and conceal my nakedness with.""**"
"8492","In another narration, when the Prophet ﷺ wore a new garment he would supplicate at the time of wearing it. > **""Praise be to Allah who has provided me from clothing what I beautify myself with among people and conceal my nakedness with.""**"
"8493","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that Hudhayfah رضي الله عنه wore new clothes and said: Praise be to Allah who concealed my nakedness and beautified me among His servants. He then said that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would say the like of that when he wore new clothes. > **""Praise be to Allah who concealed my nakedness and beautified me among His servants.""**"
"8494","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah does not bestow a blessing upon a servant who knows it is from Allah except that Allah records gratitude for him for it before he even praises Him for it; no servant commits a sin then regrets it except that Allah records His forgiveness for him before he seeks forgiveness; and no servant acquires a new garment for a dinar or half a dinar then praises Allah when wearing it except that it does not reach his knees before Allah forgives him. > **""No blessing comes to a servant who knows it is from Allah except gratitude is recorded for him before he praises Him for it, no sin is followed by regret except forgiveness is recorded before he seeks it, and no new garment is praised at wearing except forgiveness comes before it reaches his knees.""**"
"8495","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ that among his Ummah are those who come to the market and buy a shirt for half a dinar or a third of a dinar, then praise Allah when wearing it, and it does not reach his knees before he is forgiven. > **""Whoever buys a shirt for half a dinar or a third of a dinar and praises Allah when wearing it is not reached by it at his knees before he is forgiven.""**"
"8496","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Wear turbans; you will increase in forbearance.""**"
"8497","Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah reports from his father رضي الله عنه that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Wear turbans; you will increase in forbearance.""**"
"8498","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turbaned Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf رضي الله عنه and let down for him four fingers' length, and said: When I ascended to heaven I saw most of the angels wearing turbans. > **""When I ascended to heaven I saw most of the angels wearing turbans.""**"
"8499","Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, reports that when the Prophet ﷺ wore a turban he would let its end hang in front and behind."
"8500","Abdullah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that he was one of ten in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, including Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Ibn Masud, Ibn Jabal, Hudhayfah, Ibn Awf, himself and Abu Said. A young man of the Ansar came, greeted and sat. Then the Prophet ﷺ ordered Ibn Awf to prepare for an expedition, and he appeared wearing a black woollen turban. The Prophet ﷺ undid it and turbaned him himself, letting down about four fingers behind, and said: O Ibn Awf, wear the turban in this way, for it is more Arab and more handsome. Then he ordered Bilal to hand him the banner, praised Allah, invoked blessings on the Prophet ﷺ, and said: Take it, O Ibn Awf, and fight all together in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah, do not betray and do not mutilate, for this is the covenant of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet among you. > **""O Ibn Awf, wear the turban in this way, for it is more Arab and more handsome. Take it and fight all together in the path of Allah; fight those who disbelieve in Allah, do not betray and do not mutilate, for this is the covenant of Allah and the Sunnah of His Prophet among you.""**"
"8501","Abu Abd al-Salam reports that he asked Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore his turban. He said: He would wind the coil of his turban around his head, tuck it behind, and let it hang between his shoulders."
"8502","Abu Musa رضي الله عنه reports that Gabriel عليه السلام descended upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing a black turban with its ends let down behind him."
"8503","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Hold to turbans, for they are the mark of the angels, and let them hang behind your backs.""**"
"8504","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not appoint a governor until he had turbaned him and let down a tail for it on the right side toward the ear."
"8505","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wear a white cap."
"8506","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wear a white kummah cap."
"8507","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had only one shirt."
"8508","Ata reports that he saw Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf رضي الله عنه wearing a woollen shirt reaching to mid-calf, with his cloak striking his back."
"8509","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the sleeve of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reached to the wrist."
"8510","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that he entered the market with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, who sat with the cloth merchants and bought trousers for four dirhams. The weigher of the market weighed, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Weigh and give in excess. The weigher said: These are words I have never heard from anyone. Abu Hurayrah said to him: It suffices you in hardness toward your religion that you do not know your Prophet. So the man threw down the scale and rushed to kiss the hand of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, but the Messenger withdrew his hand and said: What is this? Only the non-Arabs do this with their kings; I am not a king, I am but a man among you. Then he weighed generously, the Messenger took the trousers, and when Abu Hurayrah went to carry them for him he said: The owner of a thing is most entitled to carry it, unless he is weak and his Muslim brother helps him. Abu Hurayrah asked: O Messenger of Allah, do you wear trousers? He said: Yes, in travel and residence, by night and day, for I have been commanded with covering and I have found nothing more covering than them. > **""Weigh and give in excess. I am not a king, I am but a man among you. The owner of a thing is most entitled to carry it unless he is weak and his Muslim brother helps him. I have been commanded with covering and I have found nothing more covering than trousers.""**"
"8511","Ali رضي الله عنه reports that he was sitting with the Prophet ﷺ at al-Baqi on a rainy day when a woman passed on a donkey with a driver beside her. She passed through a hollow and fell, so the Prophet ﷺ turned his face away. They said: O Messenger of Allah, she is wearing trousers. He said: > **""O Allah, forgive the trouser-wearing women of my Ummah.""**"
"8512","Anas رضي الله عنه reports from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""The izar is to mid-calf or to the ankles; there is no good in what is lower than that.""**"
"8513","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the muscle of the calf of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ could be seen from beneath his izar when he wore it."
"8514","Salamah ibn al-Akwa رضي الله عنه reports that Uthman رضي الله عنه wore his izar to mid-calf and said: Such was the izar of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."
"8515","Samurah ibn Fatik رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: What an excellent youth Samurah is, if only he took from his locks and raised his izar. So Samurah did so, taking from his locks and raising his izar. > **""What an excellent youth Samurah is, if only he took from his locks and raised his izar.""**"
"8516","Khuraym ibn Fatik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: What an excellent youth Khuraym is, if only he shortened his hair and raised his izar. Khuraym said: My hair shall not pass my ears nor my izar my ankles. > **""What an excellent youth Khuraym is, if only he shortened his hair and raised his izar.""**"
"8517","Khuraym رضي الله عنه reports that he came to the Prophet ﷺ who said: O Khuraym ibn Fatik, were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man. He asked: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? One suffices me. He said: Lengthening your hair and trailing your izar. So Khuraym went, cut his hair and shortened his izar. > **""Were it not for two traits in you, you would be the man: lengthening your hair and trailing your izar.""**"
"8518","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Wear the izar as you have seen the angels wear it. They asked: O Messenger of Allah, how did you see? He said: > **""To the middle of their calves.""**"
"8519","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that he entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing an izar that rattled on the ground. He asked: Who is this? He said: Abdullah. He said: If you are Abdullah, raise your izar. So he raised it to mid-calf, and his izar remained so until he died. > **""If you are Abdullah, raise your izar.""**"
"8520","In another narration Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه said: My izar sometimes hangs loose. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""You are not among them.""**"
"8521","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clothed him with a striped hullah gifted by Fayruz. He wore the izar and it overwhelmed him in length and width, and wore the cloak wrapped around him, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took him by the shoulder and said: O Abdullah, raise the izar, for whatever of the izar below the ankles touches the ground is in the Fire. Abdullah ibn Muhammad said: I never saw anyone more careful in raising his garment than Abdullah ibn Umar. > **""O Abdullah, raise the izar, for whatever of the izar below the ankles touches the ground is in the Fire.""**"
"8522","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whatever of the izar is below the ankles is in the Fire.""**"
"8523","Amr ibn Fulan al-Ansari رضي الله عنه reports that while he was walking with his izar trailing, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ caught up with him, holding his own forelock and saying: O Allah, Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant. Amr said: I said, O Messenger of Allah, I am a man with thin calves. He said: O Amr, Allah عزوجل has made beautiful everything He created. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck with four fingers of his right palm below the knee of Amr and said: O Amr, this is the place of the izar. Then he raised it, struck four fingers below the first place and said: O Amr, this is the place of the izar. Then he raised it and placed it below the second and said: O Amr, this is the place of the izar. > **""O Allah, Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant. O Amr, Allah has made beautiful everything He created. O Amr, this is the place of the izar.""**"
"8524","Al-Sharid رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man dragging his izar and said: Raise your izar and fear Allah. He said: I am knock-kneed with colliding knees. He said: Raise your izar, for all of Allah's creation is beautiful. Thereafter the man was never seen except with his izar at mid-calf. > **""Raise your izar and fear Allah. Raise your izar, for all of Allah's creation is beautiful.""**"
"8525","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that while they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Amr ibn Zurarah al-Ansari caught up with them in a hullah of izar and cloak, trailing it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ took hold of the edge of his garment, humbled himself to Allah and said: O Allah, Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant, until Amr heard it and turned to the Prophet ﷺ saying: O Messenger of Allah, I have thin calves. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: O Amr ibn Zurarah, Allah has made beautiful everything He created; Allah does not love the one who trails his garment. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his palm below his own knee and said: O Amr ibn Zurarah, this is the place of the izar. Then he raised it and placed it below that and said: O Amr, this is the place of the izar. > **""O Allah, Your servant, son of Your servant, son of Your maidservant. O Amr ibn Zurarah, Allah has made beautiful everything He created; Allah does not love the one who trails his garment. This is the place of the izar.""**"
"8526","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whatever of the izar is below the ankles is in the Fire.""**"
"8527","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Everything of the izar that passes beyond the ankles is in the Fire.""**"
"8528","The tailor who cut a shirt for al-Husayn ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما reports that he asked: Shall I make it to the top of the foot? He said: No. He asked: Shall I make it below the ankles? He said: Whatever is below the ankles is in the Fire."
"8529","Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه saw a Bedouin praying with his izar trailing and said: One who trails his izar in prayer is not with Allah in anything lawful or unlawful."
"8530","Hubayb ibn Mughfil رضي الله عنه saw Muhammad al-Qurashi stand dragging his izar, so Hubayb said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever treads it in arrogance treads it into the Fire.""**"
"8531","Ata ibn Yasar reports from one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ that while a man was praying with his izar trailing, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Go and perform ablution. He went, performed ablution and returned, and the Prophet ﷺ again said: Go and perform ablution. When asked why he ordered him to renew ablution then fell silent, he said: He was praying while trailing his izar, and Allah تبارك وتعالى does not accept the prayer of a servant who trails his izar. > **""Go and perform ablution. Allah تبارك وتعالى does not accept the prayer of a servant who trails his izar.""**"
"8532","Buraydah رضي الله عنه reports that they were with the Prophet ﷺ when a man of Quraysh advanced strutting in his hullah. When he stood before the Prophet ﷺ, he said: > **""O Buraydah, this is among those for whom Allah shall set no scale on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8533","Jabir ibn Abdillah رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them while they were gathered and said: O assembly of Muslims, fear Allah and join your kin, for no reward is swifter than the reward of kinship; beware of transgression, for no punishment is swifter; beware of disobedience to parents, for the fragrance of Paradise is found from a thousand years' journey, and by Allah the disobedient, the cutter of kin, the aged adulterer and the one who drags his izar in arrogance shall not find it. Pride belongs only to Allah, Lord of the worlds. All lying is sin except what benefits a believer or repels a debt. In Paradise there is a market wherein nothing is bought or sold except images; whoever loves an image of a man or woman enters into it. > **""Fear Allah and join your kin. Beware of transgression and disobedience to parents. Pride belongs only to Allah, Lord of the worlds. All lying is sin except what benefits a believer or repels a debt.""**"
"8534","Kurayb reports that he was leading Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما in the alley of Abu Lahab when Ibn Abbas asked whether they had reached such-and-such place. When told they were there, he narrated from al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib رضي الله عنه that while he was with the Prophet ﷺ in that spot, a man came strutting between two cloaks, gazing at his sides, self-conceited, whereupon Allah caused the earth to swallow him in that place, and he sinks therein until the Day of Resurrection."
"8535","Abu Said رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: While a man among those before you went out in two green cloaks strutting in them, Allah commanded the earth and it seized him, and he sinks therein until the Day of Resurrection. > **""While a man among those before you went out in two green cloaks strutting in them, Allah commanded the earth and it seized him, and he sinks therein until the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8536","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: While a man among those before you went out in two cloaks and strutted in them, Allah commanded the earth and it seized him, and he sinks therein until the Day of Resurrection. > **""While a man among those before you went out in two cloaks and strutted in them, Allah commanded the earth and it seized him, and he sinks therein until the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8537","Jabir رضي الله عنه, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ, reports that a man in a red hullah strutted and boasted in it, so Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he sinks therein until the Day of Resurrection. > **""A man in a red hullah strutted and boasted in it, so Allah caused the earth to swallow him, and he sinks therein until the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8538","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""While a man was looking at his sides, self-conceited, the earth sank with him until the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8539","Abdullah ibn Mughaffal رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The izar of the believer is to mid-calf; there is no harm in what is between it and the ankles, and what is lower than that is in the Fire.""**"
"8540","Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever drags his garment in pride, Allah shall not look at him on the Day of Resurrection, even if he is noble to Allah.""**"
"8541","Abu Ishaq reports that he saw men among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing their izars to mid-calf, naming Ibn Umar, Zayd ibn Arqam, Usamah ibn Zayd and al-Bara ibn Azib رضي الله عنهم."
"8542","Umar رضي الله عنه reports that the wives of the Prophet ﷺ were mentioned as to how much they should let down of their garments. He said: A handspan. They said: A handspan is little, the nakedness may show. He said: Then a forearm. They said: Their feet will show. He said: > **""A forearm, and no more than that.""**"
"8543","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ made one of his wives stand and measured out a handspan or two from her train and said: > **""Do not exceed this.""**"
"8544","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ measured a handspan for Fatimah رضي الله عنها from her heel and said: > **""This is the train of a woman.""**"
"8545","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Wearing the cloak is the dress of the Arabs, and wrapping up is the dress of faith, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to wrap himself. > **""Wearing the cloak is the dress of the Arabs, and wrapping up is the dress of faith.""**"
"8546","Abu Qirsafah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clothed him with a burnus hooded cloak and said: > **""Wear it.""**"
"8547","Humayd ibn Rabiah al-Qurashi reports that he saw Abu Umamah al-Bahili and al-Miqdam ibn Madikarib رضي الله عنهما wearing burnuses."
"8548","Umm Shihab al-Ghanawiyyah رضي الله عنها reports that she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he ordered barley meal for her and clothed her with a cloak."
"8549","Hibban ibn Jaz as-Salami reports from Jaz that he came to the Prophet ﷺ with a captive who had been with him among the Companions taken when they were polytheists, then they embraced Islam and brought the captive to the Prophet ﷺ. So the Prophet clothed Jaz with two cloaks, Jaz embraced Islam before him, and he said: Enter upon Aishah and she will give you two of the cloaks with her. So he entered upon Aishah, Mother of the Believers, and said: May Allah brighten you; choose for me two of these cloaks with you, for the Prophet of Allah ﷺ has clothed me with two of them. She stretched out a long arak toothstick and said: Take this and take this; the women of the Arabs in those days were not seen. > **""Enter upon Aishah and she will give you two of the cloaks with her.""**"
"8550","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah created Paradise white, and the most beloved thing to Allah is white.""**"
"8551","Al-Hasan, thinking it from Anas, reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Hold to white garments; let your living wear them and shroud your dead in them.""**"
"8552","Imran ibn Husayn and Samurah ibn Jundub رضي الله عنهما report that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Wear white; shroud your dead in it.""**"
"8553","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Hold to white garments; wear them and shroud your dead in them.""**"
"8554","Qudamah al-Kilabi رضي الله عنه reports that he saw the Prophet ﷺ on the evening of Arafah wearing a hibarah striped hullah."
"8555","Al-Hasan reports that Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه intended to forbid tamattu in Hajj, but Ubayy رضي الله عنه said to him: That is not for you; we performed tamattu with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, so Umar fell silent. He also intended to forbid hibarah striped hullahs because they are dyed with urine, but Ubayy said to him: That is not for you; the Prophet ﷺ wore them and we wore them in his time."
"8556","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ and asked: Does your Lord dye? He said: > **""Yes, with a dye that does not fade: neither red nor yellow nor white.""**"
"8557","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes dye his cloak and izar with saffron or wars and then go out in them."
"8558","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave concession for dyed garments so long as they shed nothing and carry no repellent trace."
"8559","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that Uthman رضي الله عنه set out for Makkah as a pilgrim, while the wife of Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib came to him and he spent the night with her until morning. Then he came with perfume lingering on him and a saffron-dyed muffled cloak, catching the people at Malal before they departed. When Uthman saw him he scolded him and said: Do you wear saffron-dyed clothes when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade it? Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه said to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade neither him nor you; he forbade only me."
"8560","Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa رضي الله عنه reports that the most beloved dye to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was yellow."
"8561","Qays at-Tamimi رضي الله عنه reports that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a yellow garment and saw him greeting women."
"8562","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ loved green; or he said: The most beloved colour to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was green."
"8563","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ had a blanket dyed with wars and saffron with which he would go around to his wives; if it was the night of one, he would sprinkle it with water, and if of another, she would sprinkle it with water."
"8564","Abdullah ibn Jafar رضي الله عنهما reports that he saw upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two yellow garments."
"8565","Abu Yala narrates from him that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in two garments dyed with saffron: a cloak and a turban."
"8566","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had a blanket dyed with wars which he would wear in his house, go around to his wives in it, and pray in it."
"8567","Imran ibn Muslim reports that he saw Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه wearing a yellow izar."
"8568","Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Beware of red, for it is the most beloved adornment to Satan.""**"
"8569","Rafi ibn Yazid al-Thaqafi رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Satan loves red, so beware of red and every garment of fame.""**"
"8570","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that he never saw anyone more handsome than the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a red hullah."
"8571","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that she saw Gabriel عليه السلام wearing a red turban let down between his shoulders."
"8572","Rashid al-Himmani reports that he saw Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه wearing red fur, who said: Such were our blankets at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; we wore them and prayed in them."
"8573","Sahl ibn Sad رضي الله عنه reports that a hullah of black wool with two white wool tassels was woven for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He came out to the gathering wearing it, struck his thigh and said: Do you not see how fine this hullah is? A Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, clothe me with this hullah, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never said no to anything asked of him. He said: Yes. Then he called for two cloaks, wore them, gave the hullah to the Bedouin, ordered another like it to be woven, and died while it was still being woven. > **""Do you not see how fine this hullah is? Yes.""**"
"8574","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that he saw the Prophet ﷺ sitting facing the Kaaba with his arms wrapped around his knees."
"8575","Abu Karimah reports that he heard Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه preaching on the pulpit of Kufah saying: O people, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Beware of the dress of monks, for whoever adopts monasticism or resembles them is not of me.""**"
"8576","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to a group of elderly Ansar with white beards and said: O assembly of Ansar, dye red and yellow and oppose the People of the Book. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book wear trousers and do not wear izars. He said: Wear trousers and wear izars and oppose the People of the Book. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book wear socks and do not wear sandals. He said: Wear socks and wear sandals and oppose the People of the Book. They said: O Messenger of Allah, the People of the Book trim their beards and enlarge their mustaches. The Prophet ﷺ said: Trim your mustaches, enlarge your beards, and oppose the People of the Book. > **""O assembly of Ansar, dye red and yellow and oppose the People of the Book. Wear trousers and wear izars. Wear socks and wear sandals. Trim your mustaches, enlarge your beards, and oppose the People of the Book.""**"
"8577","Jabir ibn Abdillah رضي الله عنهما reports that they asked: O Messenger of Allah, the polytheists wear trousers and do not wear izars. He said: You wear trousers and wear izars. They asked: The polytheists wear socks and do not wear sandals. He said: You wear socks and wear sandals, and oppose the allies of Satan in all you can. > **""Wear trousers and wear izars. Wear socks and wear sandals, and oppose the allies of Satan in all you can.""**"
"8578","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Among the honour of the believer with Allah is the cleanliness of his garment and his contentment with little.""**"
"8579","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Islam is clean, so keep clean, for none enters Paradise except the clean.""**"
"8580","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whenever Allah عزوجل bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves to see its trace upon him.""**"
"8581","Abu Raja al-Utaridi reports that Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه came out to them wearing a khazz cloak never seen on him before or after, and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When Allah عزوجل bestows a blessing upon one, Allah عزوجل loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant.""**"
"8582","Abu Said رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah is Beautiful; He loves beauty, and He loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant.""**"
"8583","Zuhayr ibn Abi Alqamah al-Dabbi رضي الله عنه reports that a man of bad appearance came to the Prophet ﷺ, who asked: Do you have wealth? He said: Yes, of every kind of wealth. He said: > **""Then let it be seen upon you, for Allah loves to see His trace upon His servant in a fine state, and He does not love misery nor feigned misery.""**"
"8584","Muhammad ibn al-Ashath reports from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Oil removes misery, clothing displays wealth, and kindness to servants humbles the enemy.""**"
"8585","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Clothing displays wealth, oil removes misery, and kindness to slaves is that by which Allah humbles the enemy.""**"
"8586","Abu Hazim رضي الله عنه reports that he came to the Prophet ﷺ in shabby appearance, and he asked: Do you have wealth? He said: Indeed, Allah has given me all wealth, of camels, cattle and sheep. He said: > **""Whoever has wealth, let it be seen upon him.""**"
"8587","Abu al-Ahwas reports from his father that he came to the Prophet ﷺ dishevelled and dusty in the appearance of a Bedouin. He asked: What wealth do you have? He said: Allah عزوجل has given me of all wealth. He said: > **""When Allah bestows a blessing upon a servant, He loves that it be seen upon him.""**"
"8588","Kurayb ibn Abraha reports that he heard Abu Rayhanah رضي الله عنه say: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Nothing of pride shall enter Paradise. A speaker said: O Messenger of Allah, I love to beautify even my whip cord and my sandal strap. The Prophet ﷺ said: That is not pride. Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty; pride is only whoever rejects the truth and despises people with his eyes. > **""Nothing of pride shall enter Paradise. That is not pride. Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty; pride is only whoever rejects the truth and despises people.""**"
"8589","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever drags his garments, Allah shall not look at him. Abu Rayhanah said: By Allah, what you narrated has distressed me, for by Allah I love beauty such that I make it in my sandal strap and my whip cord; is that pride? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah is Beautiful, He loves beauty, He loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant; but pride is whoever rejects the truth and despises people. > **""Whoever drags his garments, Allah shall not look at him. Allah is Beautiful, He loves beauty, and He loves to see the trace of His blessing upon His servant; but pride is whoever rejects the truth and despises people.""**"
"8590","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that he asked: O Messenger of Allah, is it pride that I have a hullah and wear it? He said: No. He asked: Is it pride that I have a mount and ride it? He said: No. He asked: Is it pride that I prepare food and invite my companions? He said: No. Pride is that you reject the truth and despise people. > **""No. Pride is that you reject the truth and despise people.""**"
"8591","Al-Husayn reports that Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما asked: O Messenger of Allah, is it pride that one of us has a noble thoroughbred camel? He said: No. He asked: Is it pride that one of us has two fine hullahs? He said: No. He asked: Is it pride that I prepare food, invite my people so they walk behind me and eat with me? He said: No. He asked: What is pride, O Messenger of Allah? He said: > **""That you reject the truth and despise people.""**"
"8592","Jabir ibn Abdillah رضي الله عنهما reports that they set out with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition. While lodging with him under a tree, he invited the Prophet ﷺ to the shade, found a young cucumber in the provision bag, and was asked whence it came. Then a man turned away wearing two worn-out garments. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at him and asked: Does he have no two garments besides these? Jabir said: O Messenger of Allah, he has two garments in the bag which you clothed him with. He said: Call him and order him to wear them. So he called him, he wore them and turned to go, and the Prophet said: What is with him? May Allah strike his neck; is not this better? The man heard it, returned and asked: O Messenger of Allah, in the path of Allah? He said: In the path of Allah. So the man was killed in the path of Allah. > **""Does he have no two garments besides these? Call him and order him to wear them. What is with him? May Allah strike his neck; is not this better? In the path of Allah.""**"
"8593","Uthman ibn Muhammad ibn Qays reports that his father saw in his hand a whip without a strap and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to a man: > **""Beautify the strap of your whip, for Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty.""**"
"8594","Sawad ibn Amr al-Ansari رضي الله عنه reports that he asked: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man to whom beauty is beloved, given of it as you see, and I dislike anyone surpassing me even in my sandal strap. Is that pride? He said: No. He asked: What is pride, O Messenger of Allah? He said: > **""Whoever rejects the truth and despises people.""**"
"8595","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty.""**"
"8596","Thabit ibn Qays رضي الله عنه reports that pride was mentioned before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was severe concerning it, saying: Allah does not love every arrogant boaster. A man said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I wash my clothes and their whiteness pleases me, my sandal strap pleases me, and my whip cord pleases me. He said: > **""That is not pride; pride is only that you reject the truth and despise people.""**"
"8597","Nufay, the freedman of Abdullah ibn Masud, reports that Abdullah رضي الله عنه was among the people with the finest white garments and the sweetest scent."
"8598","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that Tamim al-Dari رضي الله عنه bought a cloak for a thousand and used to pray in it."
"8599","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Fold your clothes and their spirits return to them, for when Satan finds a folded garment he does not wear it, and when he finds it spread out he wears it.""**"
"8600","Abu Abd al-Rahman, the foster-servant of Aishah, reports that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and Aishah رضي الله عنها in a single garment, half of it upon the Prophet ﷺ and half upon Aishah."
"8601","Abdullah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade two kinds of dress: that notorious for its beauty and that notorious for its ugliness."
"8602","Abu Said al-Tamimi reports that he heard al-Hasan and al-Husayn رضي الله عنهما say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever wears a notorious garment among clothes, Allah shall turn away from him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8603","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""There is none who wears a garment to boast in it so people look at him except that Allah shall not look at him until he removes it, whenever he removes it.""**"
"8604","Abu Yafur reports that he heard a man ask Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما: What garments shall I wear? He said: What neither the foolish despise you in nor the wise blame you for. He asked: What is that? He said: Between five dirhams and twenty dirhams."
"8605","Damrah ibn Thalabah رضي الله عنه reports that he came to the Prophet ﷺ wearing two Yemeni hullahs, and he said: O Damrah, do you think these two garments of yours will admit you into Paradise? He said: O Messenger of Allah, if you seek forgiveness for me I shall not sit until I remove them. The Prophet ﷺ said: O Allah, forgive Damrah. So he hastened until he removed them. > **""O Damrah, do you think these two garments of yours will admit you into Paradise? O Allah, forgive Damrah.""**"
"8606","Jarir ibn Abdillah رضي الله عنه said: A man may dress while naked, meaning thin garments."
"8607","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Prophet ﷺ came out having tied a knot between his shoulders, and a Bedouin asked: What is this, O Messenger of Allah? He said: > **""Woe to you, O Bedouin; I wear it only to suppress pride thereby.""**"
"8608","Abdullah ibn Sarjis رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ prayed one day in a striped namirah cloak and said to a Companion: Give me your namirah and take mine. He said: O Messenger of Allah, yours is better than mine. He said: Yes, but in it is a red thread, and I feared to look at it and be distracted. > **""Give me your namirah and take mine. In it is a red thread, and I feared to look at it and be distracted.""**"
"8609","Abu Hadrad رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Practise archery, wear coarse clothes, and walk barefoot.""**"
"8610","Abdullah ibn Abi Hadrad رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Practise archery, wear coarse clothes, walk barefoot.""** With the addition in one narration: Live hardily."
"8611","Usamah ibn Zayd رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ clothed him with a thick Coptic garment gifted by Dihyah al-Kalbi, and he clothed his wife with it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: Why have you not worn the Coptic garment? He said: O Messenger of Allah, I clothed my wife with it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Command her to place an inner lining beneath it, for I fear it may describe the size of her bones. > **""Command her to place an inner lining beneath it, for I fear it may describe the size of her bones.""**"
"8612","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: In the last of my Ummah there shall be men riding upon saddles like litters, dismounting at the doors of mosques, whose women are clothed yet naked, upon their heads like the humps of lean camels. Curse them, for they are cursed. Had there been a nation after you, your women would have served their women as the women of nations before you served you. > **""In the last of my Ummah there shall be men riding upon saddles like litters, dismounting at the doors of mosques, whose women are clothed yet naked, upon their heads like the humps of lean camels. Curse them, for they are cursed.""**"
"8613","Abu Shuqrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When you see those who cast upon their heads like the humps of cows, inform them that no prayer shall be accepted for them.""**"
"8614","Asma bint Umays رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered one day upon Aishah while her sister Asma was with her, wearing loose garments with wide sleeves. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at her he stood and left. Aishah said to her: Move aside, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw something in you he disliked. So she moved aside, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered, and Aishah asked why he stood. He said: Have you not seen her state? It is not for a Muslim woman to display of herself except thus. He took his two sleeves and covered with them the backs of his hands until nothing of his hands showed except his fingers, then raised his hands to his temples until nothing showed except his face. > **""It is not for a Muslim woman to display of herself except thus.""**"
"8615","Fatimah bint al-Walid رضي الله عنها was in Sham wearing khazz garments with an izar. It was said to her: Does this not suffice you instead of the izar? She said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ command the izar."
"8616","Maslamah ibn Makhlad رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Deprive women of outdoor garments and they will keep to their chambers.""**"
"8617","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Seek help against women through lack of outdoor clothing.""**"
"8618","Yazid ibn al-Shikhkhir reports from a Bedouin that the sandals of the Prophet ﷺ were patched."
"8619","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the sandals of the Prophet ﷺ had two straps, those of Abu Bakr had two straps, those of Umar had two straps, and the first to tie a single knot was Uthman رضي الله عنهم."
"8620","Dubaa bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had sandals with a thong strap."
"8621","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Take many sandals, for one of you remains mounted so long as he is shod.""**"
"8622","Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Take many sandals, for one of you remains mounted so long as he wears sandals.""**"
"8623","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I was commanded with sandals and the ring.""**"
"8624","Abdullah ibn Muslim ibn Hurmuz ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd ibn Ata reports from his father from his grandfather that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Strap the sandals.""**"
"8625","In another narration, a man of Taif reports from his father from his grandfather that he heard the Prophet ﷺ at Mina addressing the people, saying to them: > **""Strap the sandals.""**"
"8626","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said: Whoever wears yellow sandals continues to see joy so long as he wears them."
"8627","Dihyah al-Kalbi رضي الله عنه reports that he gifted the Messenger of Allah ﷺ a wool jubbah and two khuffs, which he wore until they tore, never asking whether their hides had been slaughtered or not."
"8628","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When my Ummah, men and women, wear patched ornate khuffs and stitch their sandals, Allah shall turn away from them.""**"
"8629","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a man wear sandals while standing."
"8630","Abu Said رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that a man walk in one sandal or one khuff."
"8631","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade that a man walk in one sandal or one khuff, spend the night alone in a house, or relieve himself in open land without bending or meeting an enemy except to shield himself."
"8632","Shaddad ibn Aws رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When the strap of one of you breaks, let him not walk in one sandal.""**"
"8633","Ali رضي الله عنه reports that when the strap of the Prophet's ﷺ sandal broke, he would walk in one sandal with the other in his hand until he found a strap."
"8634","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When you sit, remove your sandals; your feet will rest.""**"
"8635","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called for his khuffs to wear them, put on one, then a crow carried off the other and dropped it, and a snake came out of it. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear his khuffs until he shakes them out.""**"
"8636","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Only one who hopes not to wear it in the Hereafter wears silk in this world; only one with no share wears silk. Al-Hasan said: What is with people who hear this from their Prophet then place silk in their clothes and houses? > **""Only one who hopes not to wear it in the Hereafter wears silk in this world; only one with no share wears silk.""**"
"8637","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ would trace silk in garments and remove it."
"8638","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه said: O Messenger of Allah, Utarid al-Tamimi offers a silk hullah; would you buy it to wear when delegations come to you? He said: > **""Only one with no share wears silk.""**"
"8639","Habib ibn Ubayd al-Rahbi reports that Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه visited Khalid ibn Yazid, who placed a cushion for him. Abu Umamah thought it silk, so he stepped back walking backwards to the end of the row while Khalid spoke to a man. Khalid turned to Abu Umamah and asked: O my brother, did you think it silk? Abu Umamah said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""None who hopes for the days of Allah enjoys silk.""** Khalid asked: O Abu Umamah, did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? He said: O Allah, Your forgiveness; we were among a people who neither lied nor were accused of lying."
"8640","Sulayman al-Taymi reports that al-Hasan narrated the hadith of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi from Umar concerning dibaj, saying: A man of the tribe informed me that he entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing a jubbah whose facing was dibaj silk, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""A facing of Fire.""**"
"8641","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that a monk gifted the Prophet ﷺ a sundus silk jubbah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore it, then went home and removed it. Learning of a delegation coming to him, Umar رضي الله عنه urged him to wear the jubbah for their arrival. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: It is not proper for us to wear it in this world, but it is proper for us in the Hereafter; take it, O Umar. He asked: You dislike it and I take it? He said: I do not command you to wear it, but send it to the land of Persia and gain wealth thereby. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent it to the Negus, who had treated well those of the Companions who fled to him. > **""It is not proper for us to wear it in this world, but it is proper for us in the Hereafter. I do not command you to wear it, but send it to the land of Persia and gain wealth thereby.""**"
"8642","In another narration, Umar refused to take it."
"8643","Juwayriyah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever wears a garment of silk in this world, Allah عزوجل shall clothe him one day, or in a garment, of Fire on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8644","In another narration: > **""Whoever wears a garment of silk in this world, Allah shall clothe him on the Day of Resurrection in a garment of humiliation of Fire, or a garment of Fire.""**"
"8645","Abu Said or Imran رضي الله عنهما said: I bear witness upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that he forbade wearing silk."
"8646","Hudhayfah رضي الله عنه said: Whoever wears a garment of silk, Allah shall clothe him in a garment of Fire, not of your days but of the long days of Allah."
"8647","Hisham ibn Abi Ruqayyah reports that he heard Maslamah ibn Makhlad preaching from the pulpit saying: O people, do you not find in coarse and linen garments what suffices you instead of silk? Here is a man among you who shall inform you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Stand, O Uqbah. So Uqbah ibn Amir رضي الله عنه stood and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. And I bear witness that I heard him say: Whoever wears silk in this world shall be forbidden to wear it in the Hereafter. > **""Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. Whoever wears silk in this world shall be forbidden to wear it in the Hereafter.""**"
"8648","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that they were with the Prophet ﷺ when a desert man came wearing a sijan jubbah buttoned with dibaj silk, boasting that their companion sought to lower every horseman and raise every herdsman son of a herdsman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ seized the folds of his jubbah and said: > **""I shall not see upon you the dress of one without sense.""**"
"8649","Ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever wears silk in this world shall not wear it in the Hereafter.""**"
"8650","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade silk and qazz."
"8651","Abu Said al-Khudri رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them wearing a sundus silk jubbah, the most beautiful seen in a long time. Then he stood up alarmed, removed it, came out in a hibarah cloak and said: > **""Silk is the dress of the people of Paradise; whoever wears it in this world shall not wear it in the Hereafter.""**"
"8652","Muadh ibn Jabal رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ saw a jubbah bordered with silk and said: > **""A collar of Fire on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8653","Umm Hani رضي الله عنها reports that a sira striped silk hullah was gifted to the Prophet ﷺ, and he sent it to Ali. Ali came wearing it, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I am not pleased for you with what I am not pleased with for myself; I did not clothe you with it to wear it, but I clothed you with it to make it into headcovers among the Fatimahs. > **""I am not pleased for you with what I am not pleased with for myself. I did not clothe you with it to wear it, but to make it into headcovers among the Fatimahs.""**"
"8654","Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهم report that hullahs were brought to the Prophet ﷺ and he sent one to Umar. Umar came carrying it on his body and said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent me this silk hullah though you said concerning it what you said. He said: > **""I did not send it to you to wear it, but sell it and benefit from its price.""**"
"8655","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Prophet ﷺ say: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold.""**"
"8656","Hudhayfah رضi الله عنه reports that a man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: O Messenger of Allah, drought has consumed us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The world shall be opened upon you, and would that my Ummah wear nothing but dibaj.""**"
"8657","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reports that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ saying: O Messenger of Allah, drought has consumed us. He said: > **""What is other than that is more fearful to me for you: that the world be poured upon my Ummah in abundance, and would that my Ummah not wear silk.""**"
"8658","Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to them with two pouches in his hand, one of gold and one of silk, and said: > **""These two are forbidden for the males of my Ummah and lawful for the females.""**"
"8659","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ brought out in his hand a piece of gold and a piece of silk and said: > **""These two are forbidden for the males of my Ummah and lawful for their females.""**"
"8660","Zayd ibn Arqam رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Gold and silk are lawful for the females of my Ummah and forbidden for its males.""**"
"8661","Uthman رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade silk except to the measure of two fingers."
"8662","Amatullah bint Madhur reports from her mother that she visited Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها while she prayed in a shirt and headcover, and asked her about marks on clothes. She said: We used to wear such garments at the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, pointing to a garment upon her with a silk mark."
"8663","Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid reports that they were with Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه when a son of his came wearing a silk shirt. He asked: Who clothed you with this? He said: My mother. So he tore it and said: Tell your mother to clothe you with other than this."
"8664","Asma bint Abi Bakr رضي الله عنهما reports: With me are two dibaj silk sleeves of al-Zubayr which the Prophet ﷺ gave him to fight in."
"8665","Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf رضي الله عنه complained to the Prophet ﷺ of lice, so he commanded him to wear silk."
"8666","Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah reports that he saw Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Haram al-Ansari رضي الله عنه, who had prayed toward both qiblahs with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, wearing a dusty khazz garment, gesturing with his hand toward his shoulders."
"8667","Fudayl ibn Kathir reports that he saw upon Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه yellow khazz."
"8668","Salim ibn Abdillah al-Ataki reports that he saw Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه in a khazz jubbah, a cloak, a dark khazz shawl, and a black turban with its tail behind him, dyed yellow."
"8669","Mustaqim ibn Abd al-Malik reports that he saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn رضي الله عنهما wearing khazz socks of Suwar make, riding commercial mules."
"8670","Al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth reports that he saw upon al-Husayn ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما a red khazz cloak."
"8671","Al-Suddi reports that he saw al-Husayn ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما wearing a khazz turban with his hair coming out from beneath it."
"8672","Al-Shaabi reports that he visited al-Husayn ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما wearing a khazz garment."
"8673","Abu Ukashah al-Hamdani reports that he saw upon al-Husayn on the day he was killed a sundus quilted tunic."
"8674","Zurarah ibn Awfa reports that he saw Imran ibn Husayn رضي الله عنه wearing khazz."
"8675","Ammar ibn Abi Ammar reports that he saw Zayd ibn Thabit, Ibn Abbas, Abu Hurayrah and Abu Qatadah رضي الله عنهم wearing khazz shawls."
"8676","Muhammad ibn Sirin reports that khazz shawls including a red one were gifted to Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما, and he divided them among his sons."
"8677","Ikrimah reports that Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما wore khazz, and when questioned said: Only pure silk is forbidden."
"8678","Hisham ibn Urwah reports that he saw upon Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr رضي الله عنهما a green khazz shawl which Aishah had clothed him with."
"8679","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade only pure silk; what has a warp of linen or cotton, there is no harm in it."
"8680","Aidh ibn Amr رضي الله عنه used to ride striped saddles and wear khazz, seeing no harm in that."
"8681","Abdullah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the mitharah saddlecloth, qassiyyah striped silk, gold rings and mufaddam saffron-saturated garments. Yazid explained: Mitharah is skins of beasts of prey; qassiyyah is ribbed garments of silk brought from Egypt; mufaddam is saturated with saffron dye. > **""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade the mitharah, qassiyyah, gold rings and mufaddam.""**"
"8682","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade wearing silk and gold, drinking from vessels of gold and silver, red saddlecloths and wearing qassi silk. Aishah asked: O Messenger of Allah, a thin bit of gold with which to tie musk? He said: > **""No; make it of silver and yellow it with saffron.""**"
"8683","Abu al-Zubayr reports that he asked Jabir رضي الله عنه about purple mitharah saddlecloths, and he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""I do not approve it, nor wear a shirt edged with silk, nor wear qassi.""**"
"8684","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade gold rings, qassiyyah silk and red mitharah saddlecloths saturated with yellow dye."
"8685","Jadah ibn Hubayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade him three things: wearing a gold ring, wearing qassi silk, and saddlecloths."
"8686","Thawban رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade gold rings, qassiyyah silk, saffron-dyed and saturated garments, and leopard skins."
"8687","Abu Layla reports from Hariz, keeper of that house, that when he reached the Prophet ﷺ while he preached, he placed his hand upon the mitharah of his saddle and found it of ewe's skin."
"8688","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As رضي الله عنهما reports from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""Whoever of my Ummah wears gold and dies wearing it, Allah shall forbid him the gold of Paradise; whoever of my Ummah wears silk and dies wearing it, Allah shall forbid him the silk of Paradise.""** And with the addition: Whoever of my Ummah dies drinking wine, Allah shall forbid him its drink in the Hereafter."
"8689","Abu Dharr رضي الله عنه reports that while the Prophet ﷺ preached, a harsh Bedouin stood and said: O Muhammad, drought has consumed us. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""What is other than that is more fearful to me for you: when the world is poured upon you in abundance, and would that my Ummah not adorn themselves with gold.""**"
"8690","Zayd ibn Wahb reports from a man that a Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ saying: O Messenger of Allah, drought has consumed us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""What is other than drought is more fearful to me for you: the world shall be poured upon you in abundance, and would that my Ummah not wear gold.""**"
"8691","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not wear silk or gold.""**"
"8692","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever adorns himself or is adorned with a fragment of gold shall be branded with it on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8693","Sahl ibn Sad رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever loves to bracelet his child with a bracelet of Fire, let him bracelet him with gold; but silver, play with it as you wish.""**"
"8694","Usayd ibn Abi Usayd reports from Abu Musa from his father, or from Ibn Abi Qatadah from his father, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever is pleased to ring his beloved with a ring of Fire, let him ring her with gold; whoever is pleased to bracelet his beloved with a bracelet of Fire, let him bracelet her with gold; but silver, play with it in play.""**"
"8695","Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet ﷺ, reports that she asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about gold with which to tie musk. He said: > **""Make it of silver and yellow it with saffron.""**"
"8696","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade wearing gold, they asked: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not tie musk with a bit of gold? He said: > **""Why do you not tie it with silver then stain it with saffron so it is like gold?""**"
"8697","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports that she wore a necklace with strands of gold. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw it, turned away from her and said: What secures you that Allah shall not necklace you in its place on the Day of Resurrection with strands of Fire? So she removed it. > **""What secures you that Allah shall not necklace you in its place on the Day of Resurrection with strands of Fire?""**"
"8698","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports that she placed golden ornaments on her neck, and the Prophet ﷺ entered and turned away from her. She asked: Will you not look at my adornment? He said: From your adornment I turn away. They claim he said: What harms one of you to take earrings of silver then yellow them with saffron? > **""What harms one of you to take earrings of silver then yellow them with saffron?""**"
"8699","Ubadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was asked about women and their adornment. He said: > **""One brand and two brands, whatever it be.""**"
"8700","Umm al-Kiram reports that she performed Hajj and met a woman of great retinue in Makkah wearing no jewelry except silver. She asked why none of her retinue wore jewelry except silver. She said: My grandfather was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while I was with him wearing two gold earrings, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Two flames of Fire. So we are a household none of whom wears jewelry except silver. > **""Two flames of Fire.""**"
"8701","Asma bint Yazid رضي الله عنها reports that she came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pledge allegiance, drawing near with two gold bracelets upon her. He saw their glitter and said: Cast off the two bracelets, O Asma; do you not fear that Allah shall bracelet you with bracelets of Fire? She cast them off and knew not who took them. > **""Cast off the two bracelets, O Asma; do you not fear that Allah shall bracelet you with bracelets of Fire?""**"
"8702","Asma bint Yazid رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gathered the believing women for the pledge. Asma asked: Will you not uncover your hand for us, O Messenger of Allah? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: I do not shake hands with women, but I take the pledge upon them. Among the women was an aunt of hers wearing two gold bracelets and gold rings, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to her: O woman, would it please you that Allah عزوجل adorn you on the Day of Resurrection with two bracelets and rings of the embers of Hell? She said: I seek refuge with Allah, O Prophet of Allah. Asma said to her aunt: Cast off what is upon you, and she cast it off. Asma narrated: By Allah, O my son, she cast it off and none of us looked toward it nor knew who took it from its place. Asma said: I asked, O Messenger of Allah, one of us loses standing with her husband if she is not salted and adorned for him. The Prophet of Allah ﷺ said: It is nothing upon one of you to take two earrings of silver and two beads of silver, then rub them between her fingers with saffron, and they glitter as gold. > **""I do not shake hands with women, but I take the pledge upon them. Would it please you that Allah عزوجل adorn you on the Day of Resurrection with two bracelets and rings of the embers of Hell? It is nothing upon one of you to take two earrings of silver and two beads of silver, then rub them with saffron, and they glitter as gold.""**"
"8703","In a narration with Ahmad from Shahr ibn Hawshab, Asma used to serve the Prophet ﷺ. She said: While I was with him, my aunt came questioning him, wearing two gold bracelets, and the like of what preceded was mentioned."
"8704","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered while she wore two gold bracelets and said: Shall I not guide you to what is better for you than this? She said: Yes. He said: > **""Make them of silver then dye them so they are as gold.""**"
"8705","Khulaydah bint Qanab, among the women who came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to pledge, reports that a woman came wearing a gold bracelet and he refused to pledge her. She left the crowd, threw off the bracelet, returned, and he pledged her. Then she went out seeking the bracelet and found it taken."
"8706","Umm Atiyyah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them wearing gold and silvering cups. The women spoke to him about wearing gold and he refused them, but permitted them silvering cups."
"8707","Fatimah bint Qays رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade them wearing gold and stringing it. A woman threw off a gold bracelet, and it remained in the mosque for days with none taking it."
"8708","Zaynab bint Nubayt ibn Jabir, wife of Anas ibn Malik, reports that Abu Umamah enjoined her mother and aunt to go to the Prophet ﷺ. Jewelry of gold and pearls called riaath came to him, and he adorned them with riaath."
"8709","Zaynab bint Nubayt ibn Jabir reports from her mother and aunt that the Prophet ﷺ adorned them with riaath of gold."
"8710","Hammadah bint Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, eldest child of Muhammad, reports that she heard her aunt say: I found Umm Layla having her shirt, headcover and blanket dyed once every month, dyeing her hands and feet deeply with henna, saying: Upon this the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took our pledge. She said: I saw her with two bracelets of gold upon her hands, thought to be from the fay, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla would dye for her."
"8711","Umm Layla رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them: When one of you can take two bracelets of silver for her hands, let her; if she cannot, let her stain her hands even with creepers. And he said: > **""Do not resemble men.""**"
"8712","Abdullah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that his father lost his front tooth, so the Prophet ﷺ ordered him to bind it with gold."
"8713","Abdullah ibn Abdillah ibn Ubayy رضي الله عنه reports that his front tooth was injured with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he ordered him to take a tooth of gold."
"8714","Waqid ibn Abdillah at-Tamimi reports from one who saw Uthman ibn Affan رضي الله عنه capping his teeth with gold."
"8715","Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman reports that he saw al-Mughirah ibn Abdillah binding his teeth with gold."
"8716","Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman reports that he saw al-Mughirah ibn Abdillah with his teeth bound with gold, mentioned it to Ibrahim, and he said: No harm."
"8717","Sadan reports that he saw Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه being carried by his sons upon their arms around the House, with his teeth bound with gold."
"8718","Marwan ibn al-Numan reports that he saw Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه leaning upon a staff whose head was capped with silver."
"8719","Muhammad ibn Malik reports that he saw upon al-Bara رضي الله عنه a gold ring, and people asked: Why do you wear gold when the Prophet ﷺ forbade it? Al-Bara said: While we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with spoils before him of captives and household goods, he divided them until this ring remained. He raised his glance to his Companions, lowered it, raised it again, lowered it, raised it again, then said: O Bara. So I came and sat before him; he took the ring, grasped my wrist and said: Take and wear what Allah and His Messenger have clothed you with. Al-Bara would say: How do you order me to remove what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to wear? > **""O Bara. Take and wear what Allah and His Messenger have clothed you with.""**"
"8720","Ammar ibn Abi Ammar reports that Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a gold ring on a man's hand and said: Cast this off. So he cast it off and wore an iron ring. He said: This is worse than it. So he wore a silver ring and he remained silent about him. > **""Cast this off. This is worse than it.""**"
"8721","Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As رضي الله عنهما wore a gold ring, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked at it as if disliking it, so he cast it off. Then he wore an iron ring and he said: This is more vile and more vile. So he cast it off, wore a silver ring, and he remained silent about him. > **""This is more vile and more vile.""**"
"8722","In a narration with Ahmad concerning the iron ring: > **""This is the adornment of the people of the Fire.""**"
"8723","Salim ibn Abi al-Jad reports from a man of his people that he entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing a gold ring. He took a palm stalk, struck his palm with it and said: Cast it off. He went out and threw it away. He asked: What became of the ring? He said: I threw it away. He said: > **""I only ordered you to benefit from it, not to throw it away.""**"
"8724","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr and Umar did not wear their rings until Aban came to Umar, meaning they kept them but did not wear them."
"8725","Khalid ibn Sad رضي الله عنه reports that he came to the Prophet ﷺ with a ring upon his hand. The Prophet ﷺ asked: O Khalid, what is this ring? He said: A ring I have taken. He said: Hand it to me. He handed it over, and it was an iron ring overlaid with silver. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked: What is its engraving? He said: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and wore it, and it is the ring that remained in his hand. > **""O Khalid, what is this ring? Hand it to me. What is its engraving?""**"
"8726","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Abu Bakr and Umar did not wear rings nor seal letters, until Ziyad ibn Abi Sufyan wrote to Umar: You write to us things for which we find no seals. Thereupon he took a ring and sealed with it."
"8727","Ubadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""The stone of the ring of Sulayman ibn Dawud was heavenly; it was cast upon him, he took it and set it in his ring, and its engraving was: I am Allah, there is no deity but Me; Muhammad is My servant and My Messenger.""**"
"8728","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore a gold ring for three days. When his Companions saw it, gold rings spread among them, so he cast it off, none knowing what became of it. Then he took a silver ring and ordered engraved upon it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. It remained in the hand of the Prophet ﷺ until he died, in the hand of Abu Bakr until he died, in the hand of Umar until he died, and in the hand of Uthman for two years of his rule. When letters multiplied upon him, he handed it to a man of the Ansar who would seal with it. The Ansari went out to a well of Uthman and it fell from him and was never found, so he ordered a like ring made engraved: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. > **""Muhammad, Messenger of Allah.""**"
"8729","Abu Musa رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw him wearing his ring on the forefinger and middle finger and said: > **""The ring is only for this and this, meaning the little finger and the ring finger.""**"
"8730","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Prophet ﷺ wore his ring on his right, and he passed away with the ring on his right."
"8731","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ wore his ring on his right."
"8732","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ wore his ring on his right."
"8733","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ wore his ring on his right."
"8734","Jafar ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه wore his ring on his right."
"8735","Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reports that the ring of the Prophet ﷺ was upon Abu Bakr during his rule, upon Umar during his rule, and upon Uthman for part of his rule. He was at the well of Aris when the ring fell into it; they emptied the well but never found it."
"8736","Al-Saib ibn Yazid رضي الله عنه reports that the ring of the Prophet ﷺ was in the hand of Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه until he perished, then in the hand of Umar رضي الله عنه until he perished, then in the hand of Uthman رضي الله عنه until it fell into the well of Aris."
"8737","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the ring of the Prophet ﷺ was a band of silver."
"8738","Jamil ibn Abdillah reports that he saw five among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing gold rings: Zayd ibn Harithah, Zayd ibn Arqam, al-Bara ibn Azib, Anas ibn Malik and Abdullah ibn Yazid رضي الله عنهم."
"8739","Muslim ibn Abd al-Rahman reports that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pledging women at al-Safa in the year of the Conquest. A woman came whose hand was like a man's hand, and he did not pledge her until she went and changed her hands with red or yellow dye. A man came wearing an iron ring, and he said: > **""Allah does not purify a hand in which is an iron ring.""**"
"8740","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade gold rings and iron rings."
"8741","Abu Said al-Khudri رضي الله عنه reports that a man came from Bahrain to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he did not return his greeting, for upon his hand was a gold ring and a silk jubbah. The man left grieved and complained to his wife, who said: Perhaps the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked your jubbah and your ring, so cast them off. He cast them off, came the next day to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he returned his greeting. He asked: O Messenger of Allah, I came to you just now and you turned away from me? He said: In your hand was a coal of Fire. He said: Then I came with many coals. He said: What you brought is no richer to us than the stones of the lava field, but it is enjoyment of worldly life. He asked: With what shall I wear a ring? He said: > **""A band of silver, or iron, or brass. In your hand was a coal of Fire.""**"
"8742","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that a man entered upon the Prophet ﷺ wearing a brass ring. He asked: What is this ring? He said: For wahanah ailment. He said: > **""It shall only increase you in weakness.""**"
"8743","Thawban رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ passed a Companion wearing a copper ring and asked: What is the matter with this? He said: For wahanah. He said: > **""Remove it from yourself.""**"
"8744","Fatimah رضي الله عنها reports from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""Whoever wears aqeeq shall continually see good.""**"
"8745","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that one of the sons of Jafar ibn Abi Talib came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saying: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, send with me one who will buy sandals and a ring for me. So the Prophet ﷺ called Bilal and said: Go to the market, buy him sandals, buy them new and not black, and buy him a ring whose stone is aqeeq. > **""Go to the market, buy him sandals, buy them new and not black, and buy him a ring whose stone is aqeeq.""**"
"8746","Mujahid said: A woman among the early women would make for her shirt a button in her finger with which she covered her ring."
"8747","Yala ibn Murrah reports from his father that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would wipe their faces before prayer and bless them. One day he came and he wiped those to his right and left but left him, because he had visited a sister who wiped his face with yellow dye. It was said to him: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ left you only for what he saw upon your face. So he went to a well, entered it and bathed, then attended another prayer. The Prophet ﷺ passed by him, wiped his face, blessed him and said: Ala has returned with the good of his religion; he has repented and the sky has poured forth. > **""Ala has returned with the good of his religion; he has repented and the sky has poured forth.""**"
"8748","In a narration from Yala like what al-Tirmidhi narrated, with the addition: O Yala, what carried you to khaluq perfume? Have you married? He said: No. > **""O Yala, what carried you to khaluq? Have you married?""**"
"8749","Abu Habibah reports from that man that he came to the Prophet ﷺ with a need while wearing khaluq perfume. He said: Go and wash it off. He went, washed it, returned, and he again said: Go and wash it off. So he went, fell into a well, took mud and scrubbed it, then returned, and he said: Your need. > **""Go and wash it off. Your need.""**"
"8750","Yala ibn Umayyah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ married him to a woman, a hairdresser or a perfumer. He came to the Prophet ﷺ perfumed with khaluq, and he said: Will you not wash this thing? Or: Will you not wash this filth from yourself? So he went to a well, bathed in it until the water turned yellow, then entered upon the Prophet ﷺ with its trace still upon him. He said: Go and wash it. So he washed it, and it did not leave until he washed it with dust. > **""Will you not wash this thing? Will you not wash this filth from yourself? Go and wash it.""**"
"8751","Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""Three whom the angels do not approach: the sexually impure, the disbeliever, and one perfumed with saffron.""**"
"8752","Buraydah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Three whom the angels do not approach: the intoxicated, the sexually impure, and one perfumed with khaluq.""**"
"8753","Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ passed people among whom was a man perfumed with khaluq. He greeted them but turned away from the man. The man asked: O Messenger of Allah, you greeted them but turned away from me? He said: > **""Between your eyes is redness.""**"
"8754","Ali رضي الله عنه reports that a man came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge him with traces of khaluq upon him, and he refused to pledge him. So the man washed it off, returned, and he pledged him."
"8755","Umarah رضي الله عنه reports that he came to the Prophet ﷺ on the day of the Conquest of Makkah to pledge him, but seeing his hand perfumed with khaluq, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ withheld his hand from him. A man said to him: May your mother mourn you; he withheld his hand only because it is perfumed. So he washed his hand, returned to the Prophet ﷺ, and he pledged him."
"8756","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that people came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge him, among them a man with traces of khaluq upon his hand. He kept pledging them while delaying him, then said: > **""The perfume of men is what its scent shows and its colour hides; the perfume of women is what its colour shows and its scent hides.""**"
"8757","Ubadah ibn al-Samit رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man at the rear of his mosque in a saffron-dyed blanket and said: > **""Is there no man to shield between me and this Fire?""** So a man did so."
"8758","Abdullah ibn Jafar رضي الله عنهما reports that he saw upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two garments dyed with saffron: a cloak and a turban."
"8759","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would sometimes dye his cloak or izar with wars or saffron then go out in them."
"8760","Anas ibn Salman, freedman of Kab ibn Ujrah, testifies that he saw four or five among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing saffron-dyed garments, among them Kab ibn Ujrah."
"8761","Fudayl ibn Kathir reports that he saw Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه touch his forearms with khaluq from a whiteness upon him."
"8762","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ admired faghiyah henna blossoms."
"8763","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""The master basil of the people of Paradise is henna.""**"
"8764","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that while the Prophet ﷺ was at al-Uthayah, henna blossoms were brought, and he said: > **""It resembles the basil of Paradise.""**"
"8765","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When a woman perfumes herself for other than her husband, it is but Fire in disgrace.""**"
"8766","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Take condiment from this tree, meaning the olive, and whoever is offered perfume, let him take of it.""**"
"8767","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When one of you is brought perfume, let him take of it; when brought sweets, let him take of them.""** And in another wording: When perfume is placed before one of you, let him touch of it."
"8768","Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Jahsh reports from Zaynab, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ, that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Accept honour, and the best honour is perfume, light to carry and sweetest in scent.""**"
"8769","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that perfume was never offered to the Prophet ﷺ but he accepted it."
"8770","Abu Musa al-Ashari رضi الله عنه reports that a man intended to pledge the Prophet ﷺ, but the Prophet saw traces of yellow upon him and refused to pledge him, saying: > **""The perfume of men is what its scent shows and its colour hides; the perfume of women is what its colour shows and its scent hides.""**"
"8771","Abu Qays al-Awdi reports that Abdullah رضي الله عنه admired perfume."
"8772","Harb ibn al-Harith رضي الله عنه reports that he heard the Prophet ﷺ upon the pulpit on Friday saying: We have commanded wars and abar for women; as for wars, it comes to them from Yemen, and as for abar, it is taken from protected non-Muslims from their jizyah. > **""We have commanded wars and abar for women.""**"
"8773","Fadalah ibn Ubayd رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever greys a hair in Islam, it shall be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.""** A man beside him said: Some men pluck grey hair. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever wills, let him pluck his light.""**"
"8774","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that Umar would not alter his grey hair. It was said to him: O Commander of the Believers, will you not alter it when Abu Bakr used to alter? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever greys a hair in Islam, it shall be light for him on the Day of Resurrection. And we shall not alter anything. > **""Whoever greys a hair in Islam, it shall be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8775","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever greys a hair in Islam, it shall be light for him on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8776","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Do not pluck grey hair, for it is light. Whoever greys a hair in Islam, ten good deeds are written for him thereby, a sin is removed thereby, and a rank is raised thereby.""**"
"8777","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah تبارك وتعالى says: > **""I am shy of My servant and My maidservant who grey in Islam; the beard of My servant and the head of My maidservant grey in Islam, then I punish them thereafter in the Fire.""**"
"8778","Abu Malik al-Ashjai reports that he heard his father when asked: Our dye with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was wars and saffron."
"8779","Al-Hakam ibn Amr al-Ghifari رضي الله عنه reports that he and his brother Rafi ibn Amr entered upon Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه, he dyed with henna and his brother dyed yellow. Umar said to him: This is the dye of Islam, and said to his brother: This is the dye of faith."
"8780","Muhammad ibn Sirin reports that Anas رضي الله عنه was asked about the dye of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had hardly greyed except a little, but Abu Bakr and Umar after him dyed with henna and katam. He said: Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه brought his father Abu Quhafah on the day of the Conquest of Makkah carrying him until he was placed before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to Abu Bakr: Had you left the old man in his house we would have come to him in honour of Abu Bakr. So he embraced Islam with his head and beard white as thaghamah blossoms. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Change them, but avoid black.""**"
"8781","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came out to elders of the Ansar with white beards and said: O assembly of Ansar, dye red and yellow and oppose the People of the Book. > **""O assembly of Ansar, dye red and yellow and oppose the People of the Book.""**"
"8782","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Do not resemble the non-Arabs; change beards.""**"
"8783","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ commanded them with henna and forbade black."
"8784","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Dye with henna, for it increases your youth and marriage.""**"
"8785","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Change grey hair, and the best you change it with is henna and katam.""**"
"8786","Abu al-Tufayl رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The best you change grey hair with is henna and katam.""** Or he said: The Prophet ﷺ used to dye with henna and katam."
"8787","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that a man with white head and beard entered upon the Prophet ﷺ. He asked: Are you not a Muslim? He said: Yes. He said: > **""Then dye.""**"
"8788","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Dye with henna, for it is sweet in scent and settles dizziness.""**"
"8789","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that they were one day with the Prophet ﷺ when Jews entered upon him. He saw them white-bearded and asked: Why do you not change? It was said: They dislike it. The Prophet ﷺ said: > **""But you change, and beware of black.""**"
"8790","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Change grey hair and do not resemble the Jews nor the Christians.""**"
"8791","Buraydah رضي الله عنه reports that he saw henna upon the temples of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."
"8792","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah, Abu Bakr stood at his head and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah; Abu Quhafah is an aged old man at the edge of Makkah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Lead us to him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, he is more entitled to come to you. So Abu Quhafah was brought, his head and beard like white thaghamah blossoms. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Change it, but avoid black.""**"
"8793","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""In the last age there shall be people who blacken their hair; Allah shall not look at them.""**"
"8794","Umar رضي الله عنه was offered by a maidservant of his to dye his beard, and he said: Do you wish to extinguish my light as so-and-so extinguished his light?"
"8795","Abu Amir Salim ibn Amir reports that he saw Umar leave his beard unaltered."
"8796","Mustaqim ibn Abd al-Malik reports that he saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn رضي الله عنهما neither greyed nor dyeing."
"8797","Umm Ayyash رضي الله عنها said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye until he died."
"8798","Hassan ibn Abi Jabir al-Sulami رضي الله عنه reports that he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at Taif when he saw men among his Companions who had dyed their beards red and yellow. He said: > **""Welcome to those who dye red and those who dye yellow.""**"
"8799","Anas ibn Malik, Shuayb ibn Amr and Najiyah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهم said: We saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ dye."
"8800","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intended to dye, he would take oil and saffron, rub it in his hand, then work it into his beard."
"8801","Al-Jahdamah رضي الله عنها reports that she saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ come out to prayer shaking his head and beard from the traces of henna."
"8802","Utbah ibn Abd رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ would command changing hair in opposition to the non-Arabs."
"8803","Amir ibn Sad reports that Sad رضي الله عنه used to dye with black."
"8804","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that Umar ibn al-Khattab saw Amr ibn al-As with his grey blackened like a crow's wing and asked: What is this, O Abu Abdillah? He said: O Commander of the Believers, I love that some youthfulness be seen in me. He neither forbade him that nor blamed him for it."
"8805","Abu Ushshanah reports that he saw Uqbah ibn Amir رضي الله عنه dyeing black, saying: We blacken its top while its roots refuse. He was a poet."
"8806","Muhammad ibn Ali reports that he saw al-Hasan ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما dyed black upon a long-maned horse."
"8807","Sulim ibn al-Hudhayl said: I saw Jarir ibn Abdillah dyeing his head and beard black."
"8808","Muhammad ibn Ali reports that al-Husayn ibn Ali رضي الله عنهما used to dye black."
"8809","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that al-Husayn used to dye with wasimah indigo."
"8810","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah reports that he asked Abdullah ibn Abi Yazid whether he saw al-Husayn ibn Ali. He said: Yes, I saw him sitting at the basin of Zamzam. He asked: Did you see him dye? He said: No, except that I saw his head and beard black, save this spot, meaning his chin beneath the lower lip, and below that white. It is mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ had greyed in that spot of him, and he resembled him."
"8811","Abd al-Rahman ibn Buzruj reports that he saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn, sons of Fatimah رضي الله عنها, dyeing black, while al-Husayn left the chin-spot."
"8812","Abdullah ibn Abi Zuhayr said: I saw al-Husayn ibn Ali dyeing with wasimah."
"8813","Al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth said: I saw al-Hasan and al-Husayn dyeing with henna and katam."
"8814","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Whoever dyes black, Allah shall blacken his face on the Day of Resurrection.""**"
"8815","Abdullah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: > **""Yellow is the dye of the believer, red is the dye of the Muslim, and black is the dye of the disbeliever.""**"
"8816","Ismail ibn Abi Khalid said: The head of Anas ibn Malik was dyed with henna."
"8817","Ismail ibn Abi Khalid said: Anas used to yellow his beard with wars."
"8818","Uthman ibn Ubaydillah said: I saw Jabir ibn Abdillah dyeing yellow; he had witnessed al-Aqabah."
"8819","Umar ibn Abi Zaidah said: I saw Hakim ibn Jabir dyeing yellow."
"8820","Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr said: I saw Jarir dyeing yellow with saffron."
"8821","Uthman ibn Ubaydillah ibn Abi Rafi said: I saw Rafi ibn Khadij رضي الله عنه dyeing yellow."
"8822","Uthman ibn Abdillah ibn Suraqah said: I saw Abu Qatadah, Abu Hurayrah, Ibn Umar and Abu Usayd pass by them while they were in the school; the scent of amber was found from them and they yellowed their beards."
"8823","Ammar ibn Abi Ammar said: I saw Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr dyeing with henna and katam."
"8824","Ismail ibn Abi Khalid said: I saw Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa dye his beard with henna."
"8825","Muhammad ibn Ishaq said: Abdullah ibn Jafar used to dye with henna."
"8826","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Honour hair.""**"
"8827","Abu Qatadah رضي الله عنه reports from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""Whoever takes hair, let him honour it or shave it.""** Abu Qatadah used to comb his hair every other day."
"8828","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that Abu Qatadah had long locks, asked the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: > **""Honour it and oil it.""**"
"8829","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ saw a man with dishevelled head and said: > **""Why does one of you disfigure himself?""** Motioning with his hand, meaning take from it."
"8830","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ let his forelock hang as long as Allah willed him to let it, then parted it afterwards."
"8831","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""Among the felicity of the believer is lightness of his beard.""**"
"8832","Safiyyah bint Majzaah reports that Abu Mahdhurah had a lock at the front of his head which, when he sat, he let down till it reached the ground. They asked: Will you not shave it? He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over it with his hand; I shall never shave it until I die. So he never shaved it until he died."
"8833","Salim reports that he came in a delegation to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as a young boy. The Messenger ﷺ invoked blessing upon him, supplicated for him, and he purified himself from the remainder of his ablution water. That day he wore a lock, having reached or nearly reached puberty."
"8834","Hubayrah ibn Yarim said: Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه would wash his head then leave his hair behind his ears."
"8835","Abu Mamar reports that Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه had two braids, bore the appearance of the people of ignorance in simplicity, and had thin calves."
"8836","Abd al-Rahman reports that he saw al-Hasan ibn Ali رضي الله عنه with hair not reaching his shoulders."
"8837","Al-Hasan ibn Zayd reports from his father that he saw a tuft upon the head of al-Hasan, and saw al-Hasan drawing it near."
"8838","Ubayd ibn Ziyadah al-Bakri said: I visited the two sons of Bishr al-Mazini and asked: Did you see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? They said: Yes, he visited us in our dwellings; we served him food and he ate of our food. He saw coiled hairs upon the brow of one of us, placed his hand upon it and said: > **""Praise be to Allah who has placed among my Ummah the like of this.""**"
"8839","The two sons of Bishr said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon us; we spread for him a velvet cloth of ours folded, he sat, revelation descended upon him in our house, and we served him butter and dates, which he loved. Upon the head of one of them was a gathered lock like a horn, and he said: > **""Do I not see a horn among my Ummah?""**"
"8840","Amir ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr reports that Umar ibn al-Khattab when angry would twist his mustache and blow."
"8841","Hassan reports that Abu Hashim ibn Utbah had a mustache he could tie behind his nape. He asked: What is with your mustache when what came from the Prophet ﷺ concerning trimming the mustache has come? He said: I had trimmed my mustache, came to the Prophet ﷺ, and he passed his hand over it asking: When did you trim your mustache? I said: Just now. He said: > **""Then do not trim it until you meet me.""** So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ passed away before he met him, and he shall never trim it until he meets him."
"8842","Umm Ayyash رضي الله عنها said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wore his mustache close-trimmed."
"8843","Ubayd رضi الله عنه said: The Prophet ﷺ commanded close-trimming."
"8844","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Take from this and leave this, meaning take from his chin-spot and leave of his beard. > **""Take from this and leave this.""**"
"8845","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The people of polytheism enlarge their mustaches and trim their beards, so oppose them: enlarge beards and trim mustaches.""**"
"8846","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Oppose the Magians: clip mustaches and enlarge beards.""**"
"8847","Uthman ibn Ubaydillah ibn Abi Rafi reports that he saw Abu Said al-Khudri, Jabir ibn Abdillah, Abdullah ibn Amr, Salamah ibn al-Akwa, Abu Usayd al-Badri, Rafi ibn Khadij and Anas ibn Malik trimming their mustaches close as shaving, enlarging their beards, and plucking their armpits; in one narration: trimming their nails."
"8848","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man with a long mustache and said: Bring me scissors and a siwak. So he placed the siwak upon its edge and cut what exceeded. > **""Bring me scissors and a siwak.""**"
"8849","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ forbade shaving off mustaches entirely."
"8850","Al-Hakam ibn Umayr al-Yamani رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Trim the mustache with the lips.""**"
"8851","Abdullah ibn Busr رضi الله عنه reports that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ widen his mustache at the sides."
"8852","Shurahbil ibn Muslim said: I saw five among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ trimming their mustaches, enlarging their beards and yellowing them: Abu Umamah al-Bahili, al-Hajjaj ibn Amir al-Thumali, al-Miqdam ibn Madikarib, Abdullah ibn Busr and Utbah ibn Abd al-Sulami; they trimmed with the edge of the lip."
"8853","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ: > **""Among the felicity of a man is lightness of his beard.""**"
"8854","A man of Banu Ghifar reports that the Prophet ﷺ said: > **""Whoever does not shave his pubic hair, trim his nails and clip his mustache is not of us.""**"
"8855","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports from the Prophet ﷺ that it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, news of Gabriel has been slow in coming to you? He said: > **""Why should it not be slow when you around me neither use siwak, nor trim nails, nor clip mustaches, nor cleanse finger joints?""**"
"8856","Abu Wasil said: I met Abu Ayyub al-Ansari; he shook my hand, saw length in my nails and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""One of you asks about news of heaven while leaving his nails like the claws of birds wherein gather vileness, filth and dirt.""**"
"8857","Abu al-Darda رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Purifications are four: clipping the mustache, shaving pubic hair, trimming nails, and the siwak.""**"
"8858","Abdullah ibn Masud رضي الله عنه reports that they asked: O Messenger of Allah, you are deluded? He said: > **""Why should I not be deluded while the grime of one of you lies between his nail and his fingertips?""**"
"8859","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw a man with a long mustache and said: Bring me scissors and a siwak. So he placed the siwak upon its edge then took what exceeded. > **""Bring me scissors and a siwak.""**"
"8860","Mayl bint Mashrah said: I saw my father trim his nails and bury them, saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do that."
"8861","Sawadah ibn al-Rabi رضي الله عنه reports that he came to the Prophet ﷺ, who ordered camels for him, then said to him: When you return to your house, command them to feed their young stock well, command them to trim their nails so they do not wound the udders of their flocks when milking. > **""When you return to your house, command them to feed their young stock well, and command them to trim their nails so they do not wound the udders when milking.""**"
"8862","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""Enlarge beards, take from mustaches, pluck armpits, and shave the two parts.""**"
"8863","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ conquered Makkah he said: Allah and His Messenger have forbidden drinking wine and its price. He said: > **""Clip mustaches, enlarge beards, do not walk in markets except in izars; whoever acts upon the Sunnah of other than us is not of us.""**"
"8864","Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade shaving the nape except for cupping."
"8865","Abdullah ibn Amr رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade jummah flowing locks for free women and qussah tufts for slave girls."
"8866","Maqil ibn Yasar رضي الله عنه reports that a man of the Ansar married a woman whose hair had fallen out, and the Prophet ﷺ was asked about hair-joining for her. He cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman for whom it is joined."
"8867","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to curse the woman who peels faces with corrosive beautifiers and the woman for whom it is done."
"8868","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ came out with a tuft of false hair and said: > **""The women of Bani Israil used to place this in their heads, so they were cursed and the mosques were forbidden to them.""**"
"8869","Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman for whom it is joined, and the woman who tattoos and the woman who is tattooed."
"8870","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ cursed the woman who joins hair and the woman for whom it is joined."
"8871","Qays ibn Abi Hazim reports that they visited Abu Bakr رضي الله عنه in his illness and saw beside him a fair woman with tattooed hands fanning him away from him, and she was Asma bint Umays رضي الله عنها."
"8872","Bishr ibn Abdillah ibn Amr ibn Said al-Khathami reports that he visited Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn with his son beside him, who invited him to the morning meal. He said he had already eaten, and was told it was chicory. When asked what is in chicory, he narrated from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said there is no leaf of chicory except upon it a drop of the water of Paradise. Then oil was brought and he was told to oil himself. When he said he had already oiled, he was told it was violet. When asked what is in violet, he narrated from his father from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said its excellence over all oils is like the excellence of the children of Abd al-Muttalib over all Quraysh, and the excellence of violet oil is like the excellence of Islam over all religions. > **""There is no leaf of chicory except upon it a drop of the water of Paradise. The excellence of violet over all oils is like the excellence of the children of Abd al-Muttalib over all Quraysh, and the excellence of violet oil is like the excellence of Islam over all religions.""**"
"8873","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ oiled his beard he began with the chin-spot beneath the lower lip."
"8874","Lamis reports that she asked Aishah رضي الله عنها whether a woman may keep oil to endear herself to her husband, and she told her to remove from herself that which Allah does not look at. A woman said to Aishah, O my mother, and Aishah replied that she is not their mother but their sister."
"8875","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ looked into the mirror he would say praise be to Allah who made good his character and his form and adorned of him what He disfigured of others. When he applied kohl he put two in each eye and one between them. When he wore his sandals he began with the right, when he removed them he removed the left. When he entered the mosque he entered his right foot, and he loved the right in everything, in taking and giving. > **""Praise be to Allah who made good my character and my form and adorned of me what He disfigured of others.""**"
"8876","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the siwak and comb of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never left his prayer place, and he would look into the mirror when he combed his beard."
"8877","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that there are five the Messenger of Allah ﷺ never left in travel or residence: the mirror, the kohl container, the comb, the scratching stick and the siwak."
"8878","Umm al-Darda رضي الله عنها reports that she asked Aishah رضي الله عنها what she would provision the Messenger of Allah ﷺ with when she travelled with him, performed Hajj or raided with him. She said she would provision him with oil, a comb, a mirror, scissors, a kohl container and a siwak, and in one narration two pairs of scissors instead of one."
"8879","Umm Layla رضي الله عنها reports that they pledged the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and among what was taken upon them was to dye deeply, comb with honey, and never leave their hands without dye. She said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded them that when one of them can take two bracelets of silver for her hands let her, and if she cannot let her stain her hands even with creepers. > **""Dye deeply, comb with honey, never leave your hands without dye, and do not resemble men.""**"
"8880","A woman who had prayed both qiblahs with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered upon her and said dye, for one of you leaves dye until her hand is like the hand of a man. She never left dye though she reached eighty years. > **""Dye, for one of you leaves dye until her hand is like the hand of a man.""**"
"8881","Ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that women of the Ansar came to the Prophet ﷺ and he said O women of the Ansar, dye deeply, circumcise lightly without excess, for it is more beloved with your husbands, and beware the ingratitude of benefactors, meaning husbands. > **""O women of the Ansar, dye deeply, circumcise lightly without excess, for it is more beloved with your husbands, and beware the ingratitude of benefactors.""**"
"8882","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that a woman came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge him without dye upon her, and he did not pledge her until she had dyed."
"8883","Al-Sawda رضي الله عنها reports that she came to the Prophet ﷺ to pledge him and he said: > **""Go and dye, then come so I may pledge you.""**"
"8884","Muslim ibn Abd al-Rahman reports that he saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pledging women at al-Safa in the year of the Conquest. A woman came whose hand was like a man's hand, and he refused to pledge her until she went and changed her hand with yellow. A man came with an iron ring upon his hand, and he said Allah does not purify a hand in which is an iron ring. > **""Allah does not purify a hand in which is an iron ring.""**"
"8885","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""When a woman perfumes herself for other than her husband, it is but Fire in disgrace.""**"
"8886","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ said to Umm Atiyyah, a circumciser in Madinah: > **""When you circumcise, touch lightly and do not exceed, for it is brighter for the face and more beloved with the husband.""**"
"8887","Ali رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at a funeral and asked which of them would go to Madinah leaving no idol but breaking it, no grave but levelling it, and no image but defacing it. A man said he would, but feared the people of Madinah and returned. Ali said he would go, was sent, went, returned and reported he left no idol but broke it, no grave but levelled it, and no image but defaced it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said whoever returns to making anything of this has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ. Then he said do not be arrogant, nor a troublemaker, nor a trader except a trader of good, for those are the delayers of deeds. > **""Which of you will go to Madinah leaving no idol but breaking it, no grave but levelling it, and no image but defacing it? Whoever returns to making anything of this has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ. Do not be arrogant, nor a troublemaker, nor a trader except a trader of good.""**"
"8888","In another narration Ali ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man of the Ansar to level every grave and deface every idol. He said he disliked entering the houses of his people, so he sent Ali instead, and the like of the preceding was mentioned."
"8889","In another narration a man of Basrah, called Abu Muwarra by Basrans and Abu Muhammad by Kufans, mentioned the like of the first hadith without naming Ali, with the wording no image but effacing it instead of defacing it."
"8890","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ told her to sit until Gabriel came so she could greet him and he would supplicate good for her. Gabriel came, stood at the door, then returned without entering. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ asked what kept Gabriel from entering, met him at another descent and asked why he turned back from their door. Gabriel replied he had come to enter but found that small beast or figure. > **""Sit until Gabriel comes so you may greet him and he may supplicate good for you. I came to enter upon you but found that small beast or figure.""**"
"8891","Umar ibn al-Khattab رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said Gabriel promised him an appointment but was slow in coming. Then he said he was prevented only by the sound of a bell or an image in a house. > **""Gabriel promised me an appointment but was slow. I was prevented only by the sound of a bell or an image in a house.""**"
"8892","Abu Ayyub رضي الله عنه reports from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: > **""The angels do not enter a house in which is an image or a dog.""**"
"8893","Usamah ibn Zayd رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ entered the House, saw an image, called for water, began effacing it and said: > **""May Allah destroy people who picture what they do not create.""**"
"8894","Safiyyah bint Shaybah رضي الله عنها reports that she saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wet a cloth while in the Kaaba then strike with it the pictures inside."
"8895","Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنهما reports that he heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say the angels do not enter a house in which is an image of a statue, and picture-makers shall be punished in the Fire on the Day of Resurrection. The Most Merciful shall say to them rise to what you pictured, and they shall be punished until the images speak, and they shall never speak. > **""The angels do not enter a house in which is an image of a statue. Rise to what you pictured.""**"
"8896","Umm Salamah رضي الله عنها reports that she owned a gold gazelle, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered her to give it in charity, so she did."
"8897","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه, raising it to the Prophet ﷺ concerning statues, reports that he permitted what is trodden underfoot and disliked what is erected."
"8898","Abdullah ibn Umar رضي الله عنهما reports that the Prophet ﷺ passed a copper idol, struck its back with the back of his hand and said ruined and lost is whoever worships you besides Allah. Then Gabriel came to the Prophet ﷺ with an angel who withdrew. The Prophet ﷺ asked why he withdrew, and he said he smelled copper upon him, and they cannot bear the smell of copper. > **""Ruined and lost is whoever worships you besides Allah. He smelled copper upon you, and we cannot bear the smell of copper.""**"
"8899","A freedman of Aishah who led her mounts reports that when she heard the sound of a bell ahead of her she would say stop with me, and he would stop until she heard it no more. When she heard it behind her she would say hasten with me until she heard it no more. She said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it has a follower among the jinn. > **""It has a follower among the jinn.""**"
"8900","Aishah رضي الله عنها reports that on the day of Badr the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered bells cut from the necks of camels."
"8901","Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza رضي الله عنه saw a party with a bell and said the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The angels do not accompany a party in which is a bell.""**"
"8902","Hawt ibn Abd al-Uzza رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ ordered cutting bells."
"8903","Jabir رضي الله عنه reports that on a campaign he fought, the Prophet ﷺ ordered bells cut."
"8904","Anas رضي الله عنه reports that they were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when he heard the sound of a bell and said: > **""The angels do not follow a party in which is a bell.""**"
"8905","Anas ibn Malik رضي الله عنه reports that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: > **""The angels do not approach a caravan in which is a bell, nor a house in which is a bell.""**"
"8906","Abu Hurayrah رضي الله عنه reports that the Prophet ﷺ ordered bells cut."
